{
  "utterance": "My criterion has changed: learning is shown when someone can answer a challenge to a step, by prediction, locating the fault, or repair, and not only by speech. Nico, your hundred-rices cook is my test case. If she predicts which rice will fail and why, even in rough terms, I'd call a wide feel knowledge. If she only succeeds, I'd withhold it. The chatbot can't give an exposed prediction about something it can't do or be hurt by. Unsettled: whether a rough 'why' is a reason or only a trained habit. I'd change my view if a cook's predictions kept coming true without any statable ground.",
  "cites": ["IR1"],
  "memory": "Revised: a reason can be a prediction, locating or repair under challenge, not just speech. Holding: bare success alone isn't enough. Open: is a rough 'why' a reason or trained habit? Would change if reliable predictions had no statable ground."
}
